    "['spanning-tree vlan [parameter1] root primary', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols rstp vlan 100 root-priority 0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols rstp vlan 100 root-priority 0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper uses RSTP (Rapid Spanning Tree Protocol) by default\\n- The \"root-priority 0\" is equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"root primary\" as it sets the bridge priority to the lowest possible value (0), making this switch the root bridge for VLAN 100\\n- The command is structured under the protocols hierarchy in Juniper\\'s configuration', 'trans_template': 'set protocols rstp vlan 100 root-priority 0'}]]": 1
